From ee76c417ade15140b19a0904c2f8894f4cd9c7c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:31:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 839/846] wifi: b43: send A-MPDUs of up to 32 MPDUs

b43 puts at most 16 MPDUs in an A-MPDU. With 1500 byte frames at
MCS 7 that is about 3.4 ms of airtime, and each A-MPDU also costs the
RTS, the CTS, the block ack and the contention before it.

Allow 32 MPDUs. The A-MPDU stays within 4 ms of airtime and the length
the peer accepts, so at MCS 7 it ends up at about 24 MPDUs.

On an ASUS RT-N16 with an Intel 3168 client, TCP from the router goes
from 44 to 46 Mbit/s on average over three runs, open and with WPA2.

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
@@ -832,7 +832,7 @@ enum {
 					} while (0)
 
 /* Maximum number of MPDUs b43 puts in one A-MPDU */
-#define B43_AMPDU_MAX_FRAMES	16
+#define B43_AMPDU_MAX_FRAMES	32
 /* Times an MPDU missing from a block ack is sent again */
 #define B43_AMPDU_RETRY_LIMIT	5
 
